# digital.sbb.ch – SBB Design Systems

> Official guidelines of SBB (Swiss Federal Railways) for digital products: UX principles, foundations, accessibility and the design systems for websites and apps. The web design system is called Lyne and is implemented as web components (`@sbb-esta/lyne-elements`) with an Angular wrapper (`@sbb-esta/lyne-angular`).

The documentation is spread across several platforms. Use digital.sbb.ch for when and why to use a component (usage rules, elements) and for the web component API, Storybook for live examples and the Angular documentation for Angular usage. Current Lyne version: {{ lyne.version.branch }}. This file was generated on {{ buildTime }} and is rebuilt daily; if your copy is clearly older, it comes from a cache (yours or your fetch tool's), not from this server.

- [digital.sbb.ch]({{ site }}/en/): Design guidelines and usage rules (German, French, Italian, English; English and German are the most complete for Lyne)
- [Lyne Elements Storybook](https://lyne-elements.app.sbb.ch/): Web component API, live examples, code snippets; story index at https://lyne-elements.app.sbb.ch/index.json
- [Lyne Angular documentation](https://lyne-angular.app.sbb.ch/): Angular wrapper components (`@sbb-esta/lyne-angular`, `@sbb-esta/lyne-angular-experimental`) with Angular API and examples; every component page and the JSON index link to the matching Angular page
- [lyne-components on GitHub](https://github.com/sbb-design-systems/lyne-components): Source code, readme per component, issues
- [lyne-angular on GitHub](https://github.com/sbb-design-systems/lyne-angular): Source code of the Angular wrapper
- [digital.sbb.ch on GitHub](https://github.com/sbb-design-systems/digital.sbb.ch): Source of this website

Every Lyne component page below is available as Markdown (`…/index.md`) with usage rules, the elements of the component, code examples and links (Storybook, Angular); the full API tables of the web components are in `…/api.md` next to it.

A machine-readable index of all released Lyne components (elements, status such as experimental or Figma availability, and all links) is available at [{{ site }}/lyne-components.json]({{ site }}/lyne-components.json).

{% set resources = lyne.catalog.resources %}## Quick start for AI

- Install: `npm install @sbb-esta/lyne-elements` (Angular: `@sbb-esta/lyne-angular`). Components are web components with the prefix `sbb-`.
- Register elements by importing the component module once, e.g. `import '@sbb-esta/lyne-elements/button.js';` for `<sbb-button>` (one import per component group; the module path equals the component name). An element that is not imported stays an unknown, unstyled HTML element.
- Theme and tokens: load one theme stylesheet from the package, e.g. `import '@sbb-esta/lyne-elements/standard-theme.css';` (`standard-theme.css` for customer and employee applications, `off-brand-theme.css` for industry, `safety-theme.css` for safety contexts; `lean-*` variants exist for lean applications; see {{ site }}/en/design-system/lyne/themes/index.md). Style with design tokens (CSS custom properties `--sbb-*`, list: {{ site }}/en/design-system/lyne/design-tokens/index.md) instead of hard-coded colors, spacing or font sizes.
- Component details: read `…/<component>/index.md` for usage, elements and examples; the full attribute, slot and event tables are in `…/<component>/api.md`.
- Common mistakes:
  - Invented `icon-name` values. Use only names from [icons-ui.json]({{ site }}/icons-ui.json) (name plus size, e.g. `arrow-right-small`); if a name is missing there, check the authoritative catalog {{ resources.icons }}.
  - Elements that were never imported (see above) or tags that do not exist; check the component list below or lyne-components.json.
  - Wrong slots: parts such as list items, tabs or form-field inputs only work inside their parent element and often need a named slot or a specific child element; compare with the elements section and examples of the component.
  - Plain HTML attributes where Lyne expects a boolean or enum attribute (e.g. `negative`, `size="l"`); check the API table before using a value.
  - Own colors or fonts: use the theme and tokens.

## Availability of the Markdown versions

- Pages exist as `index.md` next to the HTML page (`https://digital.sbb.ch/<lang>/…/index.md`) in German and English only (French and Italian pages have no Markdown version; the content is the same, use the English or German page). Pages that only redirect (e.g. `/en/foundation/`, `/en/foundation/colors/`) have no Markdown version; use the sub pages listed below (e.g. `/en/foundation/colors/base-colors/index.md`).
- Servers answer `Accept: text/markdown` on a page URL (ending with `/`) with the Markdown version if one exists (`Vary: Accept`).
- {{ site }}/llms-full.txt is an alias of {{ site }}/lyne-components-full.md.

## Machine-readable resources

- [All Lyne components in one file]({{ site }}/lyne-components-full.md) (alias: [llms-full.txt]({{ site }}/llms-full.txt)): The Markdown versions of all released components (English) without the API tables, to load the whole context with one request
- [UI icon names]({{ site }}/icons-ui.json): All valid values for `icon-name` (name plus size, e.g. `arrow-right-small`), one entry per icon with sizes, category and keywords. Use only names from this list; do not invent icon names. It is a compact snapshot of the icon catalog, rebuilt daily; `sourceVersion` and `generated` show its state.
- [Icon catalog (authoritative)]({{ resources.icons }}): Source of all icons that Lyne loads at runtime, including timetable icons; large (about 1.2 MB, one entry per size, category and size encoded in `tags`). Use it only if a name is missing in icons-ui.json.
- [custom-elements.json]({{ resources.customElements }}): Complete API of all web components (attributes, properties, events, slots, CSS properties); experimental components: {{ resources.customElementsExperimental }}
- [Design tokens]({{ resources.designTokens }}): Colors, spacing, typography and more as JSON; as CSS custom properties: {{ resources.designTokensCss }}

